  "worked_solution": "To find a number $45%$ *greater than* $220,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+45%=145%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n145%=\\frac{145}{100}=1.45\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $45%$ greater than $220,$ we multiply $220$ by $1.45:$\n\n$$\n1.45\\cdot 220=319\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $45%$ greater than $220$ is $319.$",
